    {
      "id": "claim_0fc16191dfd74afa811c8e8a5ae60fae",
      "statement": "Setup-task deduplication is active-only: _find_setup_task(active_only=True) restricts to triage/todo/running because a 'blocked' task means 'awaiting human merge', not active work, so a finished-but-unmerged setup task must not dedup or it permanently wedges regenerate/retry flows; check_board_setup_status therefore reports pending_task_id (any non-done, for the UI badge) alongside dedup_task_id (active only, used by create_setup_task). The GitHub issues setup reuses this via create_gh_issues_setup_task, whose P0 prompt runs scripts/setup_gh_issues.py in --align mode: config.yml is always regenerated repo-aware, while bug_report.yml / feature_request.yml are rewritten only when missing or when they lack the expected 'zerofactory' label, preserving repo-customized templates.",
      "evidence": [
